# ArXiv formatting for this project

When writing or updating mathematical results in this repository:

1. Put the canonical statement in the active manuscript: `v1/paper/main.tex`
   for the frozen +1 paper, `v2/paper/main.tex` for new 2.0 results.
2. Keep detailed ledgers in `notes/`, but any claim meant to be a theorem must also appear in the LaTeX with a complete or clearly sketched proof.
3. Use standard article structure: abstract, introduction with main theorem, body lemmas, remarks/open problems, bibliography with arXiv IDs where possible.
4. Prefer self-contained proofs over “see markdown note X”; markdown is a workshop, LaTeX is the deliverable.
5. Do not announce a result as proved unless the LaTeX (or a clearly labeled conditional black-box) supports that claim.
6. After substantive math changes, update the matching `v1/` or `v2/`
   `paper/main.tex` in the same session.
